  "engine_adjustments": [
    "Native package CLI delegates to the integrated fork launcher.",
    "Installed engine assets and pyproject resolve inside this distribution.",
    "Source proof identifies the fork and packaged numerical modules separately.",
    "The core pin, flags, profiles, kernels and numerical source are preserved.",
    "Worker failure accounting handles the fork writer's skipped-batch exception.",
    "Overlapped output preserves the fork's optional confidence and structure checks.",
    "The engine reserves its output root before either prediction route launches.",
    "The worker keeps named failures distinct from complete output files.",
    "The off route accounts for named writer failures without abandoning successful records.",
    "The Python 3.14 runtime upgrade removes legacy PyTorch autocast fallbacks and preserves numerical pins.",
    "Source- and runtime-scoped sm_120 admission retains exact kernel bit checks; the fused OPM default uses a smaller shared-memory tile.",
    "On sm_120 the exact triangle block keeps the stock narrow bias projection while retaining fused Q/K/V/gate projections and epilogue."
  ],
